<BaseLayout title="About | Sowmya Narayan" description="Background, engineering focus, and professional interests of Sowmya Narayan." active="about">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">/ about</p>
    <h1>Engineer by practice.<br /><span class="accent">Curious by default.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-text">I'm Sowmya, a platform and DevOps engineer with experience building, automating, and supporting cloud infrastructure and Kubernetes-based platforms.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="content-panel prose">
    <h2>How I approach engineering</h2>
    <p>I enjoy making infrastructure more repeatable, delivery pipelines more dependable, and production systems easier to understand. My work has covered cloud platforms, infrastructure as code, CI/CD, Kubernetes operations, monitoring, and incident response.</p>
    <p>I use this site as a public engineering notebook: a place to explain technical decisions, share reproducible projects, and document lessons learned.</p>
    <h2>Areas of focus</h2>
    <ul><li>Cloud infrastructure and hybrid-cloud patterns</li><li>Kubernetes platform operations and GitOps</li><li>Terraform modules and infrastructure automation</li><li>Monitoring, alerting, troubleshooting, and reliability</li><li>Platform security, identity, and secrets management</li></ul>
    <h2>Outside the day job</h2>
    <p>Through TechGalary, I share technical learning and build hands-on projects. I also value community events and open-source collaboration as ways to learn from other engineers.</p>
    <p class="note">Before publishing, update this page with any details you want to share publicly and keep employer-specific information confidential.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
